  "conclusions": [
    "No sampled video encoding/decoding activity; no evidence of sustained GPU or memory-capacity saturation. All reports used CUDA camera matching and Windows Graphics Capture without fallback.",
    "Camera-search timing includes CPU packing, transfers, CUDA execution, synchronous readback, and result construction. It is the last search at publication time, not total CUDA time across all attempts in each frame.",
    "Late tracking intervals slowed while GPU utilization fell, not rose. Camera coordinates stopped changing in the final three reports. These intervals are not independently labeled as falls or focus changes.",
    "Windows feature recovery keeps horizontal radius 16 and vertical radius 24. Mac expands after consecutive misses to horizontal 64 and vertical 48. This path executes after the main camera solve fails.",
    "Both main camera solvers share the vertical 32-to-64 adaptive search radius and the 24-pixel recovery innovation acceptance bound. Widening the secondary recovery search alone is not proven sufficient.",
    "Both default image preprocessing paths use CPU. Mac has explicit Metal preprocessing but automatic deliberately selects CPU after its M4 measurements. Windows uploads prepared patches/luma to CUDA and downloads scores; GPU usage does not mean the whole pipeline runs on GPU."
  ],
